WEBVTT

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:36.240
Hey, where's that item we picked up the other day?

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:38.620
You asked me to carry it, remember?

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:42.460
Well, that's because your inventory is so empty.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:46.210
-Welcome back.
-You choose a quest yet?

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:47.460
Not yet.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:49.880
Hey...

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:53.590
There's a party doing the Calamity Monster Quest!

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.760
Are you serious? That's insane.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:01.890
That's a super difficult quest that a party with

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:05.600
the top members from the elite Lightning guild
only managed to beat once.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:12.690
And that's only after half of them died.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:16.280
-Nobody's tried since then.
-Can you blame them?

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.280
If your HP reaches zero, it's game over.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.040
You don't respawn, and you can't log back in.

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:26.330
Basically, it's perma-death.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:32.420
So, what reckless party is doing it?

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.420
Oh, these guys.

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:46.190
Their leader is a fighter who crushes enemies
with his powerful unique skills.

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:55.070
Their vice-leader is an all-powerful divine champion.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:07.870
There's a wizard called the Queen of Elementals for her
command of countless elementals.

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:17.050
And a shape-shifter, a dream mage,
and an empath. And...

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:20.930
-That's a full set of all six Senses.
-That's not all.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:24.430
There's one with the rare ability to see into the future.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:30.480
And when a bunch of player killers ganged up on them,

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.520
they fought them off with ease.

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:35.320
I've heard enough.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:38.570
I'd feel too unmotivated to play
if I heard any more.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:40.910
You should at least learn their names.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.970
They're the most powerful party
in Union right now.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:02.800
They're called Subaru.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.810
This is just a rumor...

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.890
I heard that their avatars have been
shape-shifted

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:12.560
and that they're in grade school in real life.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:25.280
Hey, did you hear about that new quest
called Mysteries of Darkness?

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:26.990
Mysteries of Darkness?

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.040
You heard of it, Takanori?

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:31.580
It's a recently added quest.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:34.790
Apparently, nobody has beaten it yet.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:37.130
I heard there's a crazy boss!

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.880
No, Asahi.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:42.720
I doubt the monster is that difficult.

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:45.680
The last one was a joke.

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:47.600
No, no, Clive.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:50.350
Don't you want to be the first to beat it?

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:55.440
Being able to beat a boss nobody else can
makes us cool!

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:56.770
Cool?

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:59.780
Who needs that at this point?

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:02.280
Apparently the boss is really strong.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:07.490
Every party has failed so far,
and nobody even knows how to defeat it.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.830
You heard about it too, Satsuki?

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.750
Gathering information is Adventuring 101.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:15.330
Nobody here bothers to do it.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:16.960
I see.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:21.420
That was why those Lightning members
were in such a rush.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:24.590
That I don't know. How did it turn out?

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:28.850
They made it to the boss,
but lost within ten seconds.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:30.640
That sounds like fun.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:35.730
It means we might actually get a challenge.

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:40.610
If nobody's beaten it yet,
that means we're the only ones who can!

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:41.940
Yeah!

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:45.610
Aren't you curious about
what kind of crazy attacks it has?

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:48.330
If Asahi insists that much, I'm in.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:53.120
If you're going,
then, um, I'll go as well.

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:56.170
I'm happy to finally get a challenge.

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.630
I'm a little hyped.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:00.300
So we're going?

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:03.420
We can't get anywhere without my magic.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.890
If we're doing this, we go all out.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:11.770
Make sure you bring the right items, Takanori.

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:15.810
-What did you just say to me?
-Uncle! Uncle!

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:17.060
Nozomi.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.980
That was pretty crazy yesterday.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:21.900
-Are you all okay now?
-Yeah.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:23.570
Did something happen?

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:26.070
We went to the pool together yesterday.

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:29.410
Nozomi got a cramp and almost drowned.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.910
-Let's not talk about that, Asahi.
-What to bring?

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:34.040
What's up, Satsuki?

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:36.330
Um.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:40.040
Here, Haruto!

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:41.670
What's this?

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:43.880
It's a present.

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:47.430
You can have it because I'm not using it.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.060
Get a room, you two.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:54.560
It's not like that! It's to thank him for last time.

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:56.060
You're blushing.

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:57.730
I'm not!

00:05:58.020 --> 00:05:59.650
Thanks, Satsuki.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:01.820
Let me return the favor.

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:03.690
Is there anything you want?

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:06.200
I don't need you to thank me.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:08.450
What?

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:13.200
I hope we'll always be together.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:16.460
-Of course we will be.
-Yeah.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:19.960
Although I'm the only one who can't
meet you guys IRL.

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:25.800
It doesn't matter what country you're in.
I can't imagine us being apart.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:30.720
I'd like to stay with all of you too.

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:35.850
-Looks like everyone's ready now.
-Yeah.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:39.850
This is our declaration as Subaru.

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:41.480
We trust our friends.

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:43.110
We hone our senses.

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:44.730
And we'll become stronger.

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:47.490
To shine brighter than anyone else.

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:50.110
In the name of our sworn bond.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:51.490
And...

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:53.740
Let's all become legends together!

00:06:57.290 --> 00:07:00.120
I've got items for sale here!

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:02.130
There're a lot of people here.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:06.090
We're not the only ones looking to be first.

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:08.630
Where's Haruto and Asahi?

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:10.630
I haven't seen them.

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:13.890
They're probably looking through the stalls.

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:16.390
I'll go look for them.

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:27.400
There you are. What are you...?

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:29.240
What's up, Asahi?

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:30.900
What did you want to tell me?

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:36.290
So, Haruto.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:40.790
Would you make a promise with me?

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:43.420
I...

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.790
I wonder what they're talking about.

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:47.300
So...

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:20.080
All right, let's go!

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:23.620
-What's wrong, Satsuki?
-I'm fine!

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:25.670
Are you scared or something?

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:28.210
Of course not!

00:08:51.650 --> 00:08:54.860
I thought it'd be a little harder.

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:57.700
That's just how strong we are.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:00.240
All thanks to Asahi's Prophet Art.

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:03.000
We were able to avoid many of the traps.

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:08.380
Being able to predict the future
is almost like cheating.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:11.000
It's no wonder other parties want it.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:17.510
But I only want to use this power
for you guys.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:20.760
Asahi,
we already know that.

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:24.270
Oh, right.

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:27.730
Don't worry.

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:30.770
If anybody tries to take Asahi away from us,

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:33.280
I will stop them at all costs.

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:36.320
Let's keep going and beat the boss like this.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.790
So this is the last stage.

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:48.170
Seems that way.

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:12.610
So this is Purgotorio the Darkness Pure.

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:16.070
The monster nobody has ever been able to defeat.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:17.530
Don't be scared.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:19.820
We're the invincible Subaru!

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:22.450
It's attacking from the front!

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:28.580
Takanori, take out its weapon!

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:30.330
You don't have to tell me!

00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:40.510
Breaker!

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:46.770
It didn't work! It's going to regenerate!

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:52.520
-Clive, try to match my elemental.
-Okay, Satsuki.

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:55.570
Nozomi!

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:59.150
I want to attack from above.
Can you summon a bird?

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:00.320
Yes!

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:12.290
Now, Clive!

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:13.790
Okay!

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:16.130
Activate Disaster!

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:17.800
Turn to lead!

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:22.800
That should slow it down.

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:24.220
Let's go!

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:26.180
Don't overextend, Haruto!

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:29.180
There's nothing my lion claw can't cut!

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:32.940
Come.

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:42.860
Watch out, Nozomi!

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:46.580
Oh, no!

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:07.850
No!

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:33.790
Asahi!

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:50.890
HARUTO: I CALLED ASAHI, BUT SHE'S NOT
ANSWERING.

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:53.520
CLIVE: I CAN'T BELIEVE ASAHI GOT A GAME OVER.

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:56.860
Haruto, it's your fault. You wanted to go.

00:12:57.020 --> 00:12:59.400
Everyone agreed.

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:02.610
It wouldn't have happened if Haruto didn't rush in.

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:04.610
It's not Haruto's fault.

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:06.780
If I was paying more attention...

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:09.530
It's nobody's fault.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:14.160
She must be pretty disappointed
if she's not even joining the chat.

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:17.330
We'll all need to go console her.

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:40.320
THE LATE ASAHI KUGA

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:46.110
I can't believe she died
after her character died in the game.

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:48.320
Apparently, the police came.

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:52.790
They said it was a sudden heart failure,
and the game wasn't the cause.

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:57.330
I heard the company running the game
announced that they're suspending service.

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:11.260
You...

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:14.100
You killed Asahi!

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:16.560
Stop, Takanori!

00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:17.980
Takanori.

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:30.870
I'm begging you, Amo!

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:33.660
You're the only one left.

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:37.660
-No.
-Hiyane is the only one with an account.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:39.790
You two can play alone.

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:45.010
We need to form a party of at least three people
to join the event.

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:47.470
Why me, then?

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:51.050
You had an account in grade school, didn't you?

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:53.180
For Union.

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:57.310
I heard that Union and Re'Union share accounts.

00:14:57.980 --> 00:15:00.810
I don't play those anymore.

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:02.980
I won't be any use.

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:06.530
That's fine! We just need the numbers.

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:11.320
You know how only certain people
can log into this game.

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:13.070
Sorry.

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:21.210
You're up early.

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:25.590
You always sleep in until noon
since summer vacation started.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:28.510
-Shut up.
-I didn't think you'd be up,

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:30.260
so there's only bread.

00:15:30.430 --> 00:15:32.260
That's fine. Where's Mom?

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:33.800
Shopping.

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:36.930
-I could make you some eggs.
-Thanks.

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:41.100
On to our next topic:

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:44.110
Ms. Momoi, have you heard of Re'Union?

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:46.110
Re'Union?

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:48.990
It's an MMORPG developed by

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:53.110
the internationally renowned company
Pleroma Industry.

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:57.370
In other words, it's an online game
where many people play at the same time.

00:15:57.540 --> 00:16:00.750
Here.
Your cute sister is so kind and generous.

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:05.540
Isn't this the game you used to play a long time ago?

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:06.880
No.

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:10.380
The reason this game is garnering
so much attention

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:13.050
is that players who do well in the game

00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:17.060
are given the privilege
of becoming executive candidates for Pleroma Industry,

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:22.520
receiving real-world benefits
such as study abroad opportunities and scholarships.

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:24.770
That is amazing!

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:31.240
While Re'Union is free to play,
it is not available to just anybody.

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:36.530
Only people with a special trait called "Sense"
are able to participate.

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:38.030
Sense?

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:43.540
The game first checks all applicants
to see if they have this Sense trait.

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:47.290
-That is strict.
-Thanks for breakfast.

00:16:57.140 --> 00:16:58.100
YOU RECEIVED
A MESSAGE

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:03.440
Come on, you're the only one we can turn to!

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:06.270
This afternoon's the deadline for entry.

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:07.900
Just this one time!

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:10.570
I'm begging you, do me this huge favor.

00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:17.160
Today would be six years.

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:22.080
He doesn't give up.

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:24.370
Access.

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:27.500
Play environment meets our requirements.

00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:29.590
Checking for necessary updates.

00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:32.800
Upgrading from Union to Re'Union.

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:34.800
Scanning retina.

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:36.680
Connecting to server.

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:38.260
Identity confirmed.

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:40.760
Registered user name: Haruto Amo.

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:42.520
Account confirmed.

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:45.020
Sense compatibility confirmed.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:00.030
It's a little different,

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:02.580
but it still has the eight paths.

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:07.420
Starting equipment and no bonuses.

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:09.210
My level has been reset too.

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:12.960
Not that levels mean that much here.

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:14.840
There you are!

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:17.840
You look gloomy even when you're digital.

00:18:18.010 --> 00:18:20.350
What's with the sad equipment?

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:25.100
Hey, don't get a game over before we beat the quest.

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:28.230
I promise to try.

00:18:29.480 --> 00:18:31.110
I somehow doubt that.

00:18:32.570 --> 00:18:36.740
Be careful, Amo.
It's really easy for noobs to die here.

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:40.320
A game over
means your account gets deleted immediately.

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:45.750
We're lucky enough to have the Sense to be players,
so let's avoid that please.

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:49.540
Yes, we're basically the chosen ones.

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:53.130
If things go well, we can join the elite at Pleroma.

00:18:53.290 --> 00:18:54.590
Right?

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:58.340
I would've been better off
never having that to begin with.

00:18:58.510 --> 00:19:00.430
You say something?

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:01.640
No.

00:19:02.350 --> 00:19:05.680
-I think we're close.
-I see food stalls!

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:11.520
Dungeons are pretty scary.

00:19:11.980 --> 00:19:14.270
Don't tell me this is your first time.

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:19.530
I mean,
we've only been playing for two months.

00:19:19.700 --> 00:19:22.070
It's the policy of the guild we're in.

00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:24.660
They told us to get used to the field first.

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:30.290
If you're in a guild,
you could've found a third without asking me.

00:19:30.460 --> 00:19:31.790
We did ask them!

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:34.920
They said they didn't want to do
a beginner quest.

00:19:35.090 --> 00:19:37.420
Nobody would do it with us!

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:39.760
What are your Senses?

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:42.220
-Shape-shifting.
-Magic.

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:44.550
-What about you?
-Fighter.

00:19:45.010 --> 00:19:47.100
I guess I'm the only frontline player.

00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:49.640
Here they come.

00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:53.440
-Monsters?
-They're going to be trash!

00:19:57.610 --> 00:19:59.110
Two from the front.

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:00.990
Seriously?

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:17.000
Are you, like, really good at this, Amo?

00:20:17.170 --> 00:20:19.210
Aren't you scared?

00:20:19.550 --> 00:20:21.050
I'm a fighter.

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:24.220
I can't be scared of being attacked.

00:20:24.970 --> 00:20:28.100
This would've been a lot easier before.

00:20:28.510 --> 00:20:29.640
What was that?

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:32.390
Something changed.

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:36.480
Is it me, or did the cave change?

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:43.200
Wow!

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:45.990
This made the whole trip worth it.

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:51.080
There weren't any dungeons in Union
that teleported entire spaces.

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:54.080
Probably an added feature in Re'Union.

00:20:54.250 --> 00:20:56.250
You're overthinking it too much, Amo.

00:20:56.420 --> 00:20:59.000
And it looks like there's no more monsters.

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:00.340
That's the thing.

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:03.090
I can't sense any monsters now.

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:05.130
It's like we've been isolated.

00:21:06.140 --> 00:21:08.300
Looks like a dead end.

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:11.100
The map made it seem way more complicated.

00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:13.020
We just walked straight.

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:15.940
And there weren't any traps or monsters.

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:19.150
Plus, it didn't even have a boss.

00:21:19.690 --> 00:21:21.190
What a letdown.

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:24.280
-Although, I like that it's easy.
-Is it a bug?

00:21:24.990 --> 00:21:26.780
Is that all that's here?

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:31.200
Amo, mind opening it for us?

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:33.120
Why me?

00:21:33.290 --> 00:21:36.540
Isn't it the fighter's role to open these things?

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:39.170
You can block traps with your ability.

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:42.670
Of course you'd know about stuff like that.

00:22:10.870 --> 00:22:13.080
Huh, Haruto?

00:22:13.240 --> 00:22:15.460
Asahi?

00:22:20.790 --> 00:22:24.920
Reunion and Restart

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:46.820
Seven Senses of the Re’Union

00:23:55.560 --> 00:23:57.180
Are you really Asahi?

00:23:57.390 --> 00:23:59.600
Who else could I be?

00:23:59.770 --> 00:24:02.270
-I have one basic question though...
-What is it?

00:24:02.440 --> 00:24:04.900
Why were you in a treasure chest?

00:24:05.060 --> 00:24:07.070
Episode 2, "Untold Feelings."

00:24:07.230 --> 00:24:09.360
Um...
I don't know!
